  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1974-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "From \\(p=\\log_8 3,\\) \\(\\log_2 3=3p.\\) Therefore \\[ \\log_2 5=(\\log_2 3)(\\log_3 5)=3pq. \\] Since \\(\\log_2 10=1+\\log_2 5=1+3pq,\\) \\[ \\log_{10}5=\\frac{\\log_2 5}{\\log_2 10} =\\frac{3pq}{1+3pq}. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Convert every logarithm to base \\(2\\)",
        "The givens imply \\(\\log_2 3=3p\\) and \\(\\log_2 5=3pq\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
